ba,_chiesa_della_trinit%C3%A0,_esterno_02.jpg"}},{"id":"addis_ababa_sebastopol","areaId":"addis_ababa","name":"Sebastopol","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":9.02705,"lng":38.75167},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"addis_ababa_sebastopol","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":8,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":3023,"wikidataSitelinks":4,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["sebastopol","addisababa"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Sebastopol was the name of a large artillery mortar commissioned by the Ethiopian Emperor Tewodros II (1818–1868). The name was taken from the Crimean town of Sevastopol, the site of a battle during the Crimean War. The mortar weighed approximately 6.7 tons, and was capable of firing off half-ton artillery rounds.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sebastopol (mortar)","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Tewodros_II_Sebastopol.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Tewodros_II_Sebastopol.jpg","w":1200,"h":895,"author":"Unknown but obviously died 70 years ago","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tewodros_II_Sebastopol.jpg"}},{"id":"addis_ababa_st_george_s_cathedral","areaId":"addis_ababa","name":"St. George's Cathedral","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":9.03669,"lng":38.75142},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"addis_ababa_st_george_s_cathedral","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":10,"wikiPageviews":905,"wikidataSitelinks":20,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["stgeorgescathedral","addisababa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"14:00","close":"18:00"}]},"summary":"Saint George's Cathedral is an Ethiopian Orthodox