:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Entoto Maryam Church is one of the oldest Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Churches on the Entoto Hills, 2.5 km away from Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. It was built in 1877 by Emperor Menelik II and the burial place of Menelik and his wife Empress Taytu. Several royal artifacts of the emperor and empress also found in this church.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Entoto Maryam Church","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Entoto_Maryam_Church_in_Addis_Ababa.jpg/1280px-Entoto_Maryam_Church_in_Addis_Ababa.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Entoto_Maryam_Church_in_Addis_Ababa.jpg/500px-Entoto_Maryam_Church_in_Addis_Ababa.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Ninaras","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entoto_Maryam_Church_in_Addis_Ababa.jpg"}},{"id":"addis_ababa_arat_kilo_monument","areaId":"addis_ababa","name":"Arat Kilo Monument","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":9.03285,"lng":38.7633},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"addis_ababa_arat_kilo_monument","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":4,"commonsNearby":3,"wikiPageviews":158,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["aratkilomonument","addisababa"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Arat Kilo Monument is a historic monument located in Adwa St, Arat Kilo, Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. The monument was built by Emperor Haile Selassie in 1930 during his coronation but removed during the Italian administration in 1936, and was restored in 1949 with decorations.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Arat Kilo Monument","photo":{"url